course: dictionary
lesson: 4563
title: Measuring land with hectares
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A hectare is a unit for measuring area, which is how much flat ground a shape covers. One hectare is 10,000 square metres, the size of a square 100 metres long and 100 metres wide.
explain: Picture that square on a field. It is a bit larger than a football pitch. Farmers, park keepers and foresters use hectares to say how big their land is, and the short form is ha.
explain: «Whipsnade, near London, covers about 240 hectares.» That means the zoo is about 240 squares, each as big as a 100 metre by 100 metre square. The word hectares is plural because there is more than one.
fact: A hectare is a metric unit of area.
fact: One hectare is 10,000 square metres.
fact: A square 100 metres by 100 metres is one hectare.
fact: The symbol for hectare is ha, as in 5 ha.
fact: Hectares are used to measure farms, forests and parks, as in «hectares of land» and «per hectare».
exercise: «Whipsnade, near London, covers about 240 hectares.» What is one hectare? | 1,000 metres long | 10 square metres | *10,000 square metres | 100 square kilometres
exercise: A square field is 100 metres long and 100 metres wide. How many hectares is it? | One hundred hectares | Ten hectares | *One hectare | Half a hectare
exercise: What is the short symbol for hectare? | hect | m2 | *ha | hc
test: A farmer has 12 hectares of land. Which is the best way to say it? | *12 hectares | 12 square metres | 12 hours | 12 metres long
test: The park is 3 ha. Which word means the same as ha? | metre | acre pitch | *hectare | kilogram
exam: Why is a hectare a good unit for a large forest, and how big is one hectare compared with a square of 100 metres by 100 metres? | A hectare is a weight, the same as 100 kilograms | A hectare is a time, equal to 100 minutes | A hectare is a short length, and it equals 100 metres | *A hectare is a large area, and one hectare is exactly a 100 metre by 100 metre square
